# Day 1: Define RV32I CPU Architecture

## Project

**PPA-Driven RTL-to-GDSII Implementation of a RISC-V CPU**

---

## 1. Objective

The objective of Day 1 is to freeze the architectural specification of the RISC-V CPU before beginning RTL implementation.

The CPU will implement the **RV32I base integer instruction set** using a **32-bit single-cycle microarchitecture**. The design will be developed as synthesizable SystemVerilog RTL and subsequently taken through synthesis, physical design, timing analysis, and final GDSII generation.

The architecture is intentionally kept simple, deterministic, and synthesis-friendly so that the project can focus on **power, performance, and area (PPA) optimization**.

---

## 2. ISA Selection

The selected ISA is:

**RV32I**

RV32I is the 32-bit base integer instruction set architecture.

### ISA parameters

| Parameter              | Specification     |
| ---------------------- | ----------------- |
| ISA                    | RV32I             |
| XLEN                   | 32 bits           |
| Integer registers      | 32                |
| Register width         | 32 bits           |
| `x0` behavior          | Hardwired to zero |
| Base instruction width | 32 bits           |
| Address width          | 32 bits           |
| Instruction alignment  | 4 bytes           |

