## 4. Microarchitecture

The selected CPU microarchitecture is:

> **32-bit single-cycle RISC-V processor**

Each instruction completes its complete datapath operation within one clock cycle.

The basic execution sequence is:

```text
FETCH
  ↓
DECODE
  ↓
REGISTER READ
  ↓
EXECUTE
  ↓
MEMORY ACCESS (if required)
  ↓
WRITEBACK
  ↓
NEXT PC
```

### Reason for selecting a single-cycle architecture

A single-cycle architecture was selected because it:

* reduces control complexity;
* simplifies RTL development;
* simplifies functional verification;
* provides a clear datapath for academic analysis;
* allows the project to concentrate on RTL-to-GDSII implementation and PPA optimization.

A pipelined architecture is considered future work and is not part of the baseline implementation.

