## 11. Memory Architecture

The CPU uses a **Harvard-style memory organization** with separate instruction-memory and data-memory interfaces.

```text
                    +----------------+
                    |    RV32I CPU   |
                    +-------+--------+
                            |
              +-------------+-------------+
              |                           |
              v                           v
      Instruction Memory             Data Memory
```

The physical memory arrays are kept outside the CPU core.

### Instruction memory interface

```text
imem_addr
imem_rdata
```

### Data memory interface

```text
dmem_addr
dmem_wdata
dmem_rdata
dmem_re
dmem_we
dmem_byte_en
```

The full memory architecture is specified separately in:

```text
docs/memory_architecture.md
```

