## 13. Clock and Reset

The processor uses:

```text
clk
rst
```

The baseline reset strategy is a synchronous active-high reset.

The Program Counter and sequential CPU state are initialized during reset.

The memories are external to the CPU and are therefore not part of the CPU reset state.

---

## 14. Control Architecture

The instruction decoder acts as the main control unit.

The decoder generates control signals that determine:

* ALU operation;
* ALU operand selection;
* register write enable;
* memory read enable;
* memory write enable;
* memory byte enables;
* writeback source;
* branch operation;
* jump operation;
* next-PC selection.

Conceptually:

```text
                 instruction
                      |
                      v
               +-------------+
               |   Decoder   |
               +------+------+
                      |
        +-------------+-------------+
        |      |       |      |     |
        v      v       v      v     v
      ALU    Reg     Mem    WB    PC/Branch
      Ctrl   Write   Ctrl   Sel    Ctrl
```

---

## 15. Writeback Architecture

The writeback path selects the value that is written to the destination register.

Possible writeback sources are:

```text
1. ALU result
2. Data-memory load result
3. PC + 4
```

Conceptually:

```text
ALU result --------\
                    \
Memory data --------> Writeback MUX → Register File
                    /
PC + 4 ------------/
```

